title: 'Studio UX validated end-to-end: drag-drop → per-file transcripts → clean canvas → delete cascade'
summary: |-
  Closed the full v1 UX testing arc. Studio drag-drop ingest now works cleanly: drop a video → it lands in media/<basename>, transcribes via whisper-cpp + auto-resolved large-v3-turbo model, writes per-file transcript at transcripts/<stem>.json, composes into project.atelier with one fresh source-video layer + caption layer set, and renders live in the canvas. Multi-media works: dropping a second video DOES NOT overwrite the first's transcript, DOES NOT stack stale layers, DOES NOT create root source.<ext> anymore. Right-click context menus + media-preview Delete button + floating confirmation modal (centered, backdrop-blurred, destructive-button styled) all wired and operational. The four-bug closure: (1) duplicate transcripts from "skip if exists" guard on source.<ext> copy, (2) sidebar showing root source.<ext> as a phantom duplicate of media/<basename>, (3) caption layer stacking across ingests, (4) JSON.parse-only path failing on YAML-saved project.atelier. Architectural improvement: transcribeProject now takes an optional sourcePath, so multi-media ingest passes media/<basename> directly instead of copying to source.<ext>. Project surface stays clean: just DESIGN/SCRIPT/STORYBOARD + project.atelier + media/ + transcripts/ + .atelier/.</summary>
