  <learnings>["The 'restart studio to pick up changes' loop is real friction — every node-side code change requires a process restart. Future work: hot-reload server endpoints OR clear documentation that this is expected. The Vite-served browser hot-reloads JS but the Node-side HTTP handlers are baked into the running process.", "Save-and-restore pattern for transcribeProject's root transcript.json is cleaner than dryRun bypass — dryRun also skipped rewriteCaptionLayers which we DO want for the current ingest. Save → run → mirror → restore preserves both invariants (root unchanged, captions land).", "Pre-clean stale layers before adding new ones is essential for re-entrant ingest flows. Without it, each compose accumulates source-video-N + caption-N+M layers, producing the 'overlapping text' canvas-stacking bug.", "transcribeProject's sourcePath override is the architecturally correct fix for multi-media (vs the source.<ext> copy hack). The override threads through cleanly and removes a whole class of legacy-compat clutter from creator-visible state."]</learnings>
